  "title": "All Deformation Maps in Example 8.7 of Extending Structures for n-Lie Algebras",
  "batch_label": "75",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let n >= 4 and let K be a characteristic-zero field. In the n-Lie matched-pair structure of Example 8.7 fixed in source.md and problem.md, write a linear map r: V -> g in the stated column convention as R = [[A,v],[w^T,alpha]]. Then r is a deformation map if and only if det(A) v = 0 and det(R) = alpha det(A). Equivalently, when det(A) != 0 one has v = 0 with w and alpha arbitrary, while when det(A) = 0 the sole condition is det(R) = 0.",
